  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Turnip (stalk market) prices refresh twice daily and peak between 200–600 Bells per turnip—always check prices at Timmy & Tommy's before 12:00 noon and again before 10:00 PM to catch both daily price windows.",
      "Villager friendship accelerates through daily gift-giving (one gift per day per villager adds 3–5 friendship points vs. 1 from conversation alone)—write letters with attached gifts for an extra +1 per letter.",
      "Rocks produce materials (iron, gold, stone, clay) only when hit consecutively—eat a fruit beforehand to break rocks that are inconveniently placed, then replant a replacement rock in an accessible layout.",
      "The 3-star island rating required for K.K. Slider's visit demands: 7+ villagers, 30+ furniture items outdoors, 160+ trees, 80+ flowers, and full fencing around all development areas. Check the current rating via Isabelle.",
      "Fossils spawn daily (4 per day) regardless of whether you dig the previous day's fossils—but unfound fossils disappear and do not stack. Check the entire island boundary each day before talking to other NPCs."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "カブの価格は1日2回更新され、カブ1個あたり200〜600ベルでピークになる。午前12時前と午後10時前にタヌキ商店で価格を必ず確認し、1日2回の価格ウィンドウを把握する。",
      "住人との友達度は毎日のプレゼント（住人1人につき1日1回で友達度3〜5ポイント加算、会話だけの1ポイントより高い）で加速する。手紙にプレゼントを添付すれば手紙1通につき+1ポイント追加。",
      "岩は連続して叩いた時のみ素材（鉄・金・石・粘土）を生み出す。邪魔な場所にある岩は果物を食べてから壊し、アクセスしやすいレイアウトで岩を植え直す。",
      "けKKのライブ来島に必要な島の評価3つ星には：住人7人以上・屋外家具30個以上・木160本以上・花80本以上・全開発エリアへの完全フェンス設置が必要。しずえで現在の評価を確認する。",
      "化石は前日の化石を掘ったかどうかに関係なく毎日4個出現するが、未発見の化石は消えて積み重ならない。他のNPCと話す前に島の境界全体を毎日確認する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "First Week Island Development",
        "body": "In the first real-time week, focus entirely on unlocking Nook's Cranny (requires Tom Nook's crafting quest completion, 30 hardwood, 30 softwood, 30 wood, 30 iron nuggets, and 10 pieces of furniture), the Museum (donate 15 unique fossils, fish, and bugs), and the Resident Services upgrade. These three buildings unlock the core game systems: the Museum provides daily donation rewards, Nook's Cranny offers consistent price windows, and Resident Services unlocks terraforming tools."
      },
      {
        "title": "Villager Invitation Strategy",
        "body": "The first three campsite villagers are randomly assigned, but you can influence which villagers appear at Nook Miles Ticket islands by resetting (returning to title screen if you dislike the visiting villager before talking to them). The villager you want will appear consistently at a particular mystery island if you reset enough times. Priority villagers for friendship bonuses: any villager with the Smug or Peppy personality type provides the most gifts back to the player over time."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Bell Farming: Turnip and Daily Loop",
        "body": "The most efficient bell loop after the first month: sell turnips at peak price (200+ Bells), then immediately reinvest in new turnips the following Sunday. Supplementary income: money trees (bury 10,000 Bells for a guaranteed triple-return tree), daily balloon gifts (25+ bells minimum, up to 30,000 per balloon), and star fragments (collected after wishing on shooting stars during meteor showers—each fragment sells for 250 Bells or crafts into highly valuable DIY items)."
      },
      {
        "title": "DIY Recipe Collection",
        "body": "DIY recipes drop from balloon gifts, message bottles, villager interactions, and seasonal events. The Nook Shopping catalogue sells limited seasonal DIYs available only during specific months—always check the seasonal DIY section each month and purchase immediately. Rare recipes from balloon gifts appear more frequently during morning hours (4:00–5:00 AM and 8:00–9:00 AM) when balloon spawn rates peak. Mystery islands via Nook Miles Tickets also have a chance to give recipes not yet in your possession."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Island Completion and 5-Star Rating",
        "body": "Achieving 5-star island rating requires a specific scoring threshold across greenery, furniture, and overall development. Add path tiles to connect all areas (brick or stone paths count toward development score), place seasonal furniture clusters in thematic areas, and ensure every area of the island has outdoor furniture. 5-star rating triggers unique dialogue from Isabelle and unlocks the Golden Watering Can recipe—the final island improvement tool. The gold rose breeding system (watering dead black roses with the Golden Watering Can during rain) produces the highest-value tradeable flowers."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Time-travelling to skip content—Nintendo patches detect abnormal save patterns and certain seasonal items are permanently missable if accessed via time-travel rather than the correct real-time window.",
      "Selling all fossils without donating first—the Museum requires one of each unique fossil; donating before selling ensures completeness and unlocks the fossil wing rewards.",
      "Not placing furniture outdoors—the island rating system weighs outdoor furniture heavily; furniture stored in pockets contributes nothing to island development score.",
      "Ignoring the Nookazon or trade networks—rare DIY recipes, seasonal items, and specific villagers can only be obtained through player trading; connecting with the Animal Crossing community unlocks items unavailable through solo play.",
      "Missing seasonal limited items—seasonal items (cherry blossoms, fireworks, Halloween, Toy Day) are only available for 1–3 real-time weeks per year; the Nook Shopping seasonal section should be checked daily during seasonal windows."
    ],
